  <keyword>tessera.colormap</keyword>
  <short_description>Procedural-generation colormaps.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>cmap = tessera.colormap(name)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>cmap = tessera.colormap(name, n)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>name</param_name>
      <param_description>'terrain', 'fire', 'ice' or 'grayscale'.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>n</param_name>
      <param_description>Number of colors (default 256).</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>cmap</param_name>
      <param_description>An n-by-3 RGB colormap in [0, 1].</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description><p>Return a colormap tuned for procedural fields. 'terrain' runs from deep water through lowland green and mountain brown to snow; 'fire' from black through red and orange to white; 'ice' is a cool blue ramp; 'grayscale' a neutral ramp. Pass it to colormap().</p>
  <p><img src="../images/colormap.svg" align="middle" /></p></description>
  <used_function></used_function>
  <bibliography>M. Hendrikx, S. Meijer, J. van der Velden, A. Iosup, Procedural Content Generation for Games: A Survey, ACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications and Applications 9(1), 2013. DOI 10.1145/2422956.2422957.</bibliography>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>example 1</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data><![CDATA[R = tessera.fbm(256, 6, 1);
imagesc(R); axis image off; colormap(tessera.colormap('terrain'))]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
